#. ur.io's manual signing form: how to sign with btcli, the Bittensor command line tool. The command comes from the button below this text. btcli 9 asks whether to sign with the hotkey (y/n), and the answer must be n; btcli 11 asks only for the wallet name and password. WSL is Windows Subsystem for Linux. Keep n as the letter to type.
msgctxt "bittensor_manual_btcli_steps"
